  "description": "LANXIK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H76 Er3 N11 O31 Zn2 2+,2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.479-3.790 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.29-110.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn2Er3(HL)2(H2L)2(OH)2(NO3)3](NO3)2·2CH3OH (C74H84Er3N13O39Zn2). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
